{title: He Lifted Me Up}
{subtitle: Psalms 40:1–3}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Bb/D] [Cm7] | [Cm7] | [Abmaj7] [Bb7sus4] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]I waited long for the [Cm7]Lord to hear
[Abmaj7]My cry went up through the hea[Eb]vy air
He bent down low to look [Cm7]at me
[Abmaj7]And answered what I was calling [Eb]free
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He lifted me up [Abmaj7]out of the [Eb]pit
From the [Cm7]clay where I was stuck in [Bb]it
He set my [Abmaj7]feet upon a solid [Cm7]rock
And made my steps [Abmaj7]se[Bb]cure and [Eb]strong
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The mud held fast but he [Cm7]pulled me out
[Abmaj7]My fear was broken, my doubt [Eb]removed
A new song rose with[Cm7]in my mouth
[Abmaj7]To praise the God who made me [Eb]found
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Many will see and [Cm7]stand in awe
[Bb]And put their trust in [Cm7]what he gave
[Bb]Blessed is the one who [Cm7]trusts the Lord
[Abmaj7]Who turns away from the proud and [Eb]bored
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
He lifted me up [Abmaj7]out of the [Eb]pit
He made my steps [Abmaj7]se[Bb]cure and [Eb][Bb/D][Cm7]strong [Abmaj7][Eb]
{end_of_verse}
